{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_o7dgebpte5t4xyxhpkboyw6kt7gs4lshwhf5ljdpqhlmvfa4trza","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases passed, with two real bugs found and fixed in the Rust translation.\n\n## What the target actually is\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` declares `add_executable(driver src/main.c)` — an **executable**, not a shared library, and every function except `main` is `static`. `nm -D --defined-only` returns **0 symbols for both** artifacts, so there is no `.so` and no exported symbol to compare. The faithful equivalent of the FFI boundary is the **process boundary**, so all tests drive both compiled binaries as child processes (argv + stdin in; stdout/stderr/wait-status out) and never call a Rust function directly. `libloading` is still used meaningfully: `tests/dlopen_c_lib.rs` compiles `c_src/src/main.c` a second time as a `-shared -fPIC` object (without touching `c_src/`), `dlopen`/`dlsym`s its `main`, and calls it through FFI with redirected descriptors as a second independent channel to the ground truth.\n\n## Two real divergences found and fixed (C never modified)\n\n1. **SIGPIPE disposition** — Rust's runtime sets `SIGPIPE` to `SIG_IGN` before `main`, so on a broken stdout pipe the translation ignored `EPIPE` and exited **0**, while the C program is **killed by signal 13** (status 141). Fixed by restoring `SIG_DFL` at the top of `main`.\n\n2. **Stdin consumption / file offset left behind** — the translation used `std::io::stdin()` (8 KiB `BufReader`, never seeks back). glibc buffers `st_blksize` (4096) bytes and, at `exit()`, `_IO_cleanup → _IO_SYNC` hands the unconsumed read-ahead back to a *seekable* descriptor. Observable via `{ driver; cat; } < file`:\n\n   | scenario | C | Rust before | Rust after |\n   |---|---|---|---|\n   | 31-byte file | leaves ` REST-OF-DATA…` | leaves nothing | matches |\n   | 20 011-byte file | offset 5 | offset 8192 | matches |\n   | 20 011-byte pipe | consumed 4096 | consumed 8192 | matches |\n\n   Fixed with a `CStdin` stream modelling glibc's buffer size, one `read()` per underflow, buffer-index pushback, and the exit-time `sync()`.\n\n## The blind spot the mutants exposed\n\nHappy-path green was **not** sufficient: the program's stdout only reveals whether each value *equals* 1/2/3 — a 3-bit oracle — so a wrong overflow rule (wrap instead of `strtol` saturation) coincided with correct behavior on essentially every random large input. I added `tests/scan_semantics.rs`, whose inputs are engineered so each *plausible wrong* semantics lands on a magic constant while glibc does not (e.g. `2^64+1` must **not** become 1; `4294967297` must narrow **to** 1), plus a 600-case cross-check against an independent model. `run_all_configs.sh --mutants` now proves the suite bites: **15/15 behavioral mutants killed**, and the 2 survivors are documented as *provably* unobservable (`keep_scanning`: once conversion *i* fails, variable *i* keeps a default that fails its own check, and `multi_stage` returns before any later variable is read; `neg_sat_to_m1`: 0 vs −1 are both non-magic).\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- [x] **SYMBOLS.md** — `nm -D` diff empty; all three C entities (`main`, `multi_stage`, `y`) translated; no stubs.\n- [x] **Phase B** — all 31 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass over ~10 600 randomized iterations, plus an exhaustive sweep of every 1- and 2-byte stream.\n- [x] **Phase C** — all 25 `ERRORS.md` rows have passing differential tests (incl. closed/directory stdin, `/dev/full`, SIGPIPE, out-of-range values past every documented boundary).\n- [x] **Every configuration** — 67 tests × {debug, release} × {default, `--no-default-features`}, all green, 0 warnings. No `[features]`, no CMake `option()`, no `#ifdef` exists, and the script fails loudly if one is ever added."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":938,"cache_read_input_tokens":184824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":938,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"662b8b79-5378-4331-a2c1-8c397c9c2f98","uuid":"e983efb5-08e1-46ae-90ef-b9784b8fcda7","timestamp":"2026-08-18T06:11:48.834Z"}
